{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T05:07:41.297Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0760c2a023788e66016ab35e7bd70887d18cc353dc93d4d7f3","status":"completed","call_id":"call_pKnWCajrkF3J1zv4yqmjEgV1","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/ubuntu/cd3-csr-work/docs/cd3-csr-garbage.md\\n+# CSR garbage policies\\n+\\n+These experiments use the original CD3 CSR storage and decoder. Dedicated KV\\n+capacity, GPU staging capacity, and attention kernels are unchanged. The\\n+starting point is remote `origin/main` at\\n+`19a15c5d66d14481acb7e00c5e6f371d8ffb0964`.\\n+\\n+Both performance suites accept `--cd3-kv-csr-policy append|compact|reuse`.\\n+The default is `append`; the other policies require `--cd3-kv-storage csr`.\\n+Standalone callers set `TIERED_SERVE_KV_CD3_CSR_POLICY`.\\n+\\n+| Policy | Retirement | New encoded entries |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| `append` | Mark old words as garbage | Append; retain existing capacity-pressure rebuilds |\\n+| `compact` | Repack the remaining live entries after each physical retirement batch | Repack if overwriting records creates garbage; otherwise append |\\n+| `reuse` | Coalesce freed ranges and trim a free tail | Best-fit hole first, then append; rebuild on capacity/fragmentation failure |\\n+\\n+The `compact` policy publishes new pinned entries and offsets. Older plans keep\\n+their original tensors until H2D completes. It preserves allocated capacity\\n+but reduces `used_words`, which controls contiguous entries transfers. Returning\\n+memory to the OS is not required to remove garbage from H2D.\\n+\\n+The `reuse` policy uses indices ordered by address and by `(size, address)`.\\n+Adjacent free ranges merge. A remainder smaller than eight 64-bit words stays\\n+with its allocation, allowing at most 56 bytes of internal slack per such\\n+allocation. Logical entry counts remain exact. The free tail is removed from\\n+`used_words` immediately; interior holes and internal slack remain part of a\\n+contiguous entries transfer until they are reused or a rebuild occurs.\\n+\\n+Retirement only changes allocation metadata in `reuse` mode. The existing\\n+encoder waits for the layer's preceding H2D before overwriting any body or\\n+entries bytes. If an encoder is pending, physical retirement remains deferred\\n+until that writer stops. This applies to both new policies.\\n+\\n+## Measurement\\n+\\n+`cd3_csr_garbage_bytes` counts dead entries and internal slack actually included\\n+in CD3 H2D submissions. It is a subset of `cd3_gap_bytes`: the latter also\\n+includes entries of live but inactive blocks. If the existing capacity fallback\\n+packs selected entries, its transferred garbage is zero. A policy does not\\n+claim to remove live-but-inactive data.\\n+\\n+The serving suite's `--kv-byte-metrics` records per-forward byte counters\\n+without enabling GPU timing. All compared policies must use the same option.\\n+Byte totals cover all server forwards, whereas the client's request trimming\\n+only affects client latency statistics.\\n+\\n+At worker shutdown, `CD3 CSR totals` logs compaction count, bytes repacked,\\n+bytes placed in holes, bytes appended, and bytes retired. Its\\n+`sum_peak_used_bytes` is the sum of individual layer/side high-water marks,\\n+not a simultaneously measured process-memory peak.\\n+\\n+The bounded comparison uses real requests from the existing Azure trace:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+for policy in append compact reuse; do\\n+  bash scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh \\\\\\n+    --codecs cd3 --modes kvcomp \\\\\\n+    --cd3-kv-storage csr --cd3-kv-csr-policy \\\"$policy\\\" \\\\\\n+    --cd3-kv-execution serial \\\\\\n+    --chunks 8192 --request-rates 4 --max-num-seqs 64 \\\\\\n+    --dedicated-kv-blocks 2432 \\\\\\n+    --num-prompts 192 --skip-first-n-requests 16 \\\\\\n+    --skip-last-n-requests 16 --repeats 1 --kv-byte-metrics \\\\\\n+    --output-root \\\"benchmark_results/cd3_csr/$policy\\\"\\n+done\\n+```\\n+\\n+Compaction removes all dead entries but copies the live entries repeatedly.\\n+Reuse avoids most movement but can retain scattered holes. A possible follow-up\\n+is reuse with occasional compaction when measured wasted transfers justify the\\n+copy cost. A fixed threshold is a heuristic, not an optimality guarantee;\\n+the two policies above isolate the tradeoff before adding that combination.\\n*** End Patch\"));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"docker cp /home/ubuntu/cd3-csr-work/docs/cd3-csr-garbage.md tiered-serve:/root/projects/tiered-serve/docs/cd3-csr-garbage.md\",\"max_output_tokens\":500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"tail -n 6 /home/ubuntu/cd3-csr-work/append-suite.log\",\"max_output_tokens\":1700}));\ntext(await tools.clock__curr_time({}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0cc9e-4b8e-7211-ba96-c841b5155eb7","create_time":1790140011.704682}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-23T05:07:41.307Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"patch_apply_end","call_id":"exec-5ac86af3-60fd-469d-87df-a6971dc90fed","turn_id":"01a0cc9e-4b8e-7211-ba96-c841b5155eb7","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /home/ubuntu/cd3-csr-work/docs/cd3-csr-garbage.md\n","stderr":"","success":true,"changes":{"/home/ubuntu/cd3-csr-work/docs/cd3-csr-garbage.md":{"type":"add","content":"# CSR garbage policies\n\nThese experiments use the original CD3 CSR storage and decoder. Dedicated KV\ncapacity, GPU staging capacity, and attention kernels are unchanged. The\nstarting point is remote `origin/main` at\n`19a15c5d66d14481acb7e00c5e6f371d8ffb0964`.\n\nBoth performance suites accept `--cd3-kv-csr-policy append|compact|reuse`.\nThe default is `append`; the other policies require `--cd3-kv-storage csr`.\nStandalone callers set `TIERED_SERVE_KV_CD3_CSR_POLICY`.\n\n| Policy | Retirement | New encoded entries |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `append` | Mark old words as garbage | Append; retain existing capacity-pressure rebuilds |\n| `compact` | Repack the remaining live entries after each physical retirement batch | Repack if overwriting records creates garbage; otherwise append |\n| `reuse` | Coalesce freed ranges and trim a free tail | Best-fit hole first, then append; rebuild on capacity/fragmentation failure |\n\nThe `compact` policy publishes new pinned entries and offsets. Older plans keep\ntheir original tensors until H2D completes. It preserves allocated capacity\nbut reduces `used_words`, which controls contiguous entries transfers. Returning\nmemory to the OS is not required to remove garbage from H2D.\n\nThe `reuse` policy uses indices ordered by address and by `(size, address)`.\nAdjacent free ranges merge. A remainder smaller than eight 64-bit words stays\nwith its allocation, allowing at most 56 bytes of internal slack per such\nallocation. Logical entry counts remain exact. The free tail is removed from\n`used_words` immediately; interior holes and internal slack remain part of a\ncontiguous entries transfer until they are reused or a rebuild occurs.\n\nRetirement only changes allocation metadata in `reuse` mode. The existing\nencoder waits for the layer's preceding H2D before overwriting any body or\nentries bytes. If an encoder is pending, physical retirement remains deferred\nuntil that writer stops. This applies to both new policies.\n\n## Measurement\n\n`cd3_csr_garbage_bytes` counts dead entries and internal slack actually included\nin CD3 H2D submissions. It is a subset of `cd3_gap_bytes`: the latter also\nincludes entries of live but inactive blocks. If the existing capacity fallback\npacks selected entries, its transferred garbage is zero. A policy does not\nclaim to remove live-but-inactive data.\n\nThe serving suite's `--kv-byte-metrics` records per-forward byte counters\nwithout enabling GPU timing. All compared policies must use the same option.\nByte totals cover all server forwards, whereas the client's request trimming\nonly affects client latency statistics.\n\nAt worker shutdown, `CD3 CSR totals` logs compaction count, bytes repacked,\nbytes placed in holes, bytes appended, and bytes retired. Its\n`sum_peak_used_bytes` is the sum of individual layer/side high-water marks,\nnot a simultaneously measured process-memory peak.\n\nThe bounded comparison uses real requests from the existing Azure trace:\n\n```bash\nfor policy in append compact reuse; do\n  bash scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh \\\n    --codecs cd3 --modes kvcomp \\\n    --cd3-kv-storage csr --cd3-kv-csr-policy \"$policy\" \\\n    --cd3-kv-execution serial \\\n    --chunks 8192 --request-rates 4 --max-num-seqs 64 \\\n    --dedicated-kv-blocks 2432 \\\n    --num-prompts 192 --skip-first-n-requests 16 \\\n    --skip-last-n-requests 16 --repeats 1 --kv-byte-metrics \\\n    --output-root \"benchmark_results/cd3_csr/$policy\"\ndone\n```\n\nCompaction removes all dead entries but copies the live entries repeatedly.\nReuse avoids most movement but can retain scattered holes. A possible follow-up\nis reuse with occasional compaction when measured wasted transfers justify the\ncopy cost. A fixed threshold is a heuristic, not an optimality guarantee;\nthe two policies above isolate the tradeoff before adding that combination.\n"}},"status":"completed"}}
